course: dictionary
lesson: 4134
title: Glittery and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives glittery three meanings, and the sentence around the word shows which one the writer means. Read the words near it first: they are its context.
explain: «The snow lay on the hill, glittery in the morning sun.» Here glittery is about light: the snow shines with lots of tiny flashes. In «a glittery card», it means covered with glitter. In a story about a film star's party, it can mean showy and glamorous.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well. Morven, 16, borrows Iona's glittery hair clips and says, «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin.» The clips are shiny and sparkly, and braw tells you they are lovely.
fact: Glittery means covered with glitter, or shining with lots of small flashes of light.
fact: Glittery can also mean showy and glamorous, full of bright lights and fame.
fact: «Braw» (Scotland) means lovely, and «wee yin» means little one.
fact: Many schools now use eco-friendly glitter, because ordinary glitter is often tiny plastic.
fact: Useful phrases are glittery card, glittery dress and glittery nail polish.
exercise: «The snow was glittery under the moon.» What does glittery mean here? | Soft and fluffy like a cloud | Dark and gloomy | *Shining with lots of tiny flashes of light | Cold and frozen solid
exercise: Ella makes a «glittery card» for Grandad's birthday. What does glittery mean in this phrase? | Very old and dusty | *Covered with glitter, tiny shiny bits that sparkle | Torn and crumpled | Quiet and calm
exercise: Morven says, «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin.» What does braw mean? | Too big for her | Broken | *Lovely | Boring
test: «The celebrity arrived in a glittery gold dress, surrounded by cameras.» Which meaning of glittery fits best? | Cold and wet from the rain | Quiet and calm | Old and dusty from the attic | *Showy and glamorous, full of bright lights and fame
test: Why do many schools now use eco-friendly glitter? | Because glitter makes the classroom too dark | Because glitter is too heavy to stick to paper | *Because ordinary glitter is often tiny plastic that can harm the planet | Because glitter is only sold in winter
exam: Which word could replace glittery in «The glittery stars filled the night sky»? | silent | soggy | heavy | *sparkling
